  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Door 1: the tailnet",
      "items": [
        "Pi-hole answers *.platanosverdes.com with the raspi's Tailscale IP, derived from Caddy's hosts every deploy",
        "Hosts in PIHOLE_DNS_PUBLIC_HOSTS (Grafana) resolve to Cloudflare instead, so Access signs you in even here",
        "Plex is never proxied: Caddy redirects to the LAN IP, reached through the Pi's /32 subnet routes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Door 2: public behind Access",
      "items": [
        "Cloudflare edge, then Access asks for Google, then tunnel rpi reaches Caddy or an app port",
        "Tunnel routes and Access apps live in Cloudflare's dashboard, not in this repo",
        "A container label prometheus.probe.access checks that a stranger still gets the login"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Door 3: public without login",
      "items": [
        "torre (companion repo) and /hooks/deploy only",
        "The webhook checks GitHub's HMAC-SHA256 signature before anything runs",
        "It listens on 127.0.0.1:9000 and runs apply.sh only for a push to main",
        "Outside the doors: the router forwards qBittorrent's QBIT_BT_PORT for peers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Two nodes, one repo",
      "items": [
        "Both run main and their own apply.sh cron; only the raspi has the webhook and the tunnel",
        "streamhalla lists services in COMPOSE_PROFILES and loads overrides/secondary-node.yml",
        "streamhalla also runs gluetun, sleipnir (peer :8092), pushgateway, node-exporter, cAdvisor, speedtest-tracker"
      ]
    }
  ]
